    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d666">

                <pb facs="0785" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/790: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-25T23:00:00-04:00">November 25, 1942—11
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5948. Your 6574, November 21,<anchor n="30" xml:id="d666-f1"/> indicates that
                    General Hartle has approved the approach to the Irish authorities outlined in
                    the Department’s 5675<anchor n="31" xml:id="d666-f2"/> but does not clearly
                    state your own approval. If you concur in the proposal will you forward the
                    Department’s 5675 to Mr. Gray for the action contemplated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
